From: Precision GPU maintenance
Subject: [LOCAL CANDIDATE] Rebuild monitors after secondary GPU addition

Observed on Mutter 50.1: adding a GPU populates its outputs but leaves them
without MetaMonitor objects until the monitor manager reads current state.
A subsequent ApplyMonitorsConfig reaches is_connector_configured_for_lease
with a NULL monitor. The retained core confirms RDI=0 at
meta_monitor_is_for_lease+7.

Reload after successful hot-add, once the GPU and renderer have been added.
Also treat an as-yet unassociated connector as not configured for leasing.
This does not implement full GPU removal/re-add or release Xwayland handles.

--- a/src/backends/native/meta-drm-lease.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-drm-lease.c
@@ -200,6 +200,8 @@ is_connector_configured_for_lease (MetaKmsConnector *connector)
     return FALSE;
 
   monitor = meta_output_get_monitor (META_OUTPUT (output_kms));
+  if (!monitor)
+    return FALSE;
   return meta_monitor_is_for_lease (monitor);
 }
 
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-backend-native.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-backend-native.c
@@ -656,7 +656,10 @@ on_udev_device_added (MetaUdev          *udev,
           g_warning ("Failed to hotplug secondary gpu '%s': %s",
                      device_path, error->message);
         }
+      return;
     }
+
+  meta_monitor_manager_reload (meta_backend_get_monitor_manager (backend));
 }
 
 static gboolean
